  - name: Domain Warping
    author: "I\xF1igo Qu\xEDlez"
    category: 5
    licenseType: 9
    customLicenseText: 
    url: https://iquilezles.org/articles/warp/
    usageDescription: Source of the domain warping technique used to distort 3D density
      and cave noise coordinates, breaking up grid-aligned noise structure.
    sourceFiles: []
    projectFiles:
    - Assets/Scripts/Jobs/StandardChunkGenerationJob.cs
    version: 
    notes: "Article (2002). Technique only \u2014 no code used. Applied as a single
      DomainWarp() call per warp source rather than the article's recursive fbm(p
      + fbm(p + fbm(p)))."
  - name: 'GPU Gems 3, Chapter 1: Generating Complex Procedural Terrains Using the
      GPU'
    author: Ryan Geiss (NVIDIA)
    category: 5
    licenseType: 9
    customLicenseText: 
    url: https://developer.nvidia.com/gpugems/gpugems3/part-i-geometry/chapter-1-generating-complex-procedural-terrains-using-gpu
    usageDescription: "Source of the 3D density-function terrain model \u2014 positive
      density is solid, negative is air, the zero-crossing is the surface \u2014
      which replaced the 2D heightmap and enables overhangs, arches and caves."
    sourceFiles: []
    projectFiles:
    - Assets/Scripts/Jobs/StandardChunkGenerationJob.cs
    version: 
    notes: "Book chapter. Technique only \u2014 no code used. Evaluated in Burst
      on the CPU rather than on the GPU, and restricted to the Dynamic Density Band
      instead of the full volume."
